HST: HTML pasted from a web page does not become absolutely positioned frames

A block with "position: absolute" (Facebook's "text on coloured background" post, overlays,
badges) became a page-anchored frame when pasted: it covered other text and lost the background
image its light text was made for. When HTML is pasted or inserted into an existing document,
"position: absolute" is read as static, so the content flows in the text with the colour rules of
hst-writer-html-paste-readable-colors.patch. Opening an HTML file is unchanged; floats and
multi-column blocks are not affected. Hook in ParseStyleOptions (htmlcss1.cxx), logic in
sw/source/filter/html/hsthtmlpaste.cxx.

Test: CppunitTest_sw_hst_html_paste (testAbsolutePost*).

